---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ExecutionOrigin from '../../components/ExecutionOrigin.astro';
import NirDiagramPreview from '../../components/NirDiagramPreview.astro';
import PlasticityNetworkPreview from '../../components/PlasticityNetworkPreview.astro';
import { ADAPTER_SOURCE_URL } from '../../data/live-runtime';
import { labs } from '../../data/labs';
import '../../styles/labs.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Labs" description="Focused neuromorphic experiments. Each lab labels where its data comes from and stays readable without JavaScript.">
  <section class="page-intro compact" aria-labelledby="labs-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Labs</p>
    <h1 id="labs-title">Focused experiments, one question each.</h1>
    <p>Each lab isolates one part of the neuromorphic stack. Every page states where its data comes from, and none of them is the live simulation on the homepage.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="labs-index" aria-label="Available labs">
    <ol class="labs-list">
      {labs.map((lab) => (
        <li>
          <article class="lab-entry">
            <div class="lab-entry-copy">
              <ExecutionOrigin origin={lab.origin === 'live-wasm' ? 'unavailable-wasm' : lab.origin} />
              <h2><a href={lab.href}>{lab.title}</a></h2>
              <p>{lab.summary}</p>
              <ul class="technology-list" aria-label="Crates">
                {lab.crates.map((crate) => <li>{crate}</li>)}
              </ul>
              <a class="text-link" href={lab.href}>Open the lab <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
            </div>
            {lab.preview === 'nir-diagram' ? <NirDiagramPreview /> : null}
            {lab.preview === 'plasticity-network' ? <PlasticityNetworkPreview /> : null}
          </article>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>
  <section class="section" id="how-the-demo-works" aria-labelledby="how-the-demo-works-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Homepage demo</p>
    <h2 id="how-the-demo-works-title">How the live demo works.</h2>
    <p>On each live tick, nominally every 50 ms, the homepage turns your pointer, or a scripted path when nobody is interacting, into one <code>[x, y, pressure]</code> packet. <code>kinetic-signals</code> turns it into 16 features, <code>axon-encoder</code> encodes them as spikes, <code>neuromod</code> steps its LIF neurons, and <code>synaptic-wiring</code> owns the synapses and delays each pulse travels along. The <a href={ADAPTER_SOURCE_URL}>adapter crate</a> composes them into one WebAssembly module; the canvas only draws what it returns.</p>
    <p>Before WebAssembly and WebGL start, and whenever they cannot, the drawing on the homepage is the same network: it is rendered at build time from the topology the browser bridge requires of every live snapshot.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
